#---
# purpose: "an activation minted after a return component solves still gets its return answered"
#---
#
# `Map.keys/1` and `Map.to_list/1` walk the same recursive helper. Analysing
# the first mints that helper's activation and puts it in a recursive-return
# component, which solves. Analysing the second reaches the SAME helper
# activation, so it joins the component after its owner has already answered.
# The owner learns of the new member through `Callers`, re-solves, and answers
# for it too. Without that subscription nothing wakes the owner and the second
# call's return is never published.
#
# The order matters: `Map.to_list/1` first and `Map.keys/1` second does not
# exercise the late join.
def main() do
  dbg(Map.keys(%{a: 1}))
  dbg(Map.to_list(%{a: 1}))
end
